<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199bceafabf5447d6a16a2d7f513622ac689ac55a498973017d08871e204c751</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning--f18b77019ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canberra's zoo treats its residents to personnalised musical therapy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f18283a1091b5c18fa41cb6e85d5cae9dc4471ed743a3171951bcafd9b700b6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:14Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy--0d0087f76a83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy" /><summary type="html">A music therapist in Australia has been playing for animals at Canberra's zoo for the last five years. It's a relaxing experience for animals and staff alike and the animals all react differently to the music played.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal deadly floods: FRANCE 24 report – on the ground with survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fba8692eb532318b3cae5974cb439838387a457e1170f094020dee1aedad504</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:12:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-_-on-the-ground-with-survivors--b891d1208ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-%E2%80%93-on-the-ground-with-survivors" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. While rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur in the Nuwako district – one of the villages hit by the flood on August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal grapples with destruction and loss in wake of deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d7d21c7555f693b10c75c39eaba9cddbc9c162d19bc3319641a8e5261942e1</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:10:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods--17641910cea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal have warned of possible fresh flooding after water levels rose in the Bhotekoshi River. The floods took place after a glacier collapse. They have killed at least 900 people - with more than 4,000 others missing in Nepal and Tibet. Now, a massive rescue effort continues and communities grapple with devastation and loss.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find its missing as flood area remains largely inaccessible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:340dc44fed67beb7bd85eb11a4005cb17e9ec1a1d6d0d04b435a760c3075f4b7</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:56Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible--450be663b9f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rescuers are racing against the clock to find the over 4,000 people missing after the flash floods that devastated an area in the north of the country on August 26. Rescue operations include one where workers are trying to save hundreds believed to be stuck inside a blocked hydropower project. Meanwhile, authorities have started burying unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal's survivors look to rebuilding their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f9055c1a88f99f0c484e56cf2f063cde8beb4a7e02f54f8949ad371f271a3f</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:53:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives--e039613e514e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. In the devastated villages, families lost everything in minutes. And while rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur, in the Nuwako district, one of the villages hit by the flood of August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal starts burying its dead as search for over 4,200 missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:225bba5f94e8004a7d2864c7b9c9d2f0a868e6fedec57f9723455da8dafaaea2</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:45Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:33:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues--d8984474f7d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The combined deaths in Nepal and China surpassed 900, with more than 4,700 people missing. It also includes 933 workers on hydropower projects along the river which the torrent crashed through. With morgues running at full capacity, the country has started to bury unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 244s Shazaib Wahlah tells us more from a grief-stricken Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about the SCO, the summit billed as a counterweight to US influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2e5690809bc9df4498034c525292945d9f553b9c26afbcfcaa4ed7883f1e941</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence--bcde7c336260.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, Russia and India are among the heads of state gathering in Kyrgyzstan for the summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization. The summit is celebrating its 25 years in existence. Although the group is billed as a counterweight to US. global influence, it is not the case for all participating countries. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry takes a look at what the SCO is, and what will be discussed this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal rescue teams seek hundreds of workers trapped in hydropower tunnels by deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aec8fde555d402e5ea0f95166437decdb43add904598935be2bb0b7cecc3bd68</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:51Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:15:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods--361362dcb3af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Supported by experts from China and India, Nepal's rescue teams on Monday endeavoured to reach hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in hydropower tunnels blocked by the devastating flood of mud, water and debris that swept through the Himalayan region last week.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>What justice for Nepal after flooding?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76a2d7ca7b6ecd68815586f461bd4b5ab087dac0742766cf19ba3075868bad99</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:54Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T07:54:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal--ce44c0b4ecf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, August 31: The international press tell the story of a heroic headmaster in Nepal who managed to save more than 1,600 pupils, while the Nepali press lambast a lack of accountability for major polluters. Meanwhile in France, back-to-school season reopens wounds over child sex abuse in before- and after-school clubs. Finally, do ants and bees have a concept of voting?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal buries victims of Himalayan flooding as death toll climbs past 900</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59ec3c432fd5a9675e4982e118e2537c011a909a3dad29aa3d83a0446a218dea</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:57Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T05:46:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900--38c4dbe0877d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Monday began mass burials for the hundreds of people killed in catastrophic flash floods along the Nepal-Tibet border last week, as authorities announced the death toll had climbed past 900 people. Officials in Nepal and neighbouring China are still searching for more than 4,000 missing people, including hundreds of hydropower plant workers across the remote Himalayan region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Week in pictures: devastating floods in Nepal, death of Dolly Parton and a tornado in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56220648c818b91c27020fbb77452f1c4e4f9e93b26e747a4d17886790b992bc</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:47:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france--6e7418132498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images: a devastating flood tears through Nepal and Tibet, the death of global icon Dolly Parton, a tornado devastates a village in southern France and the Humanoid Robot World Games in China offers a peek at the future.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c992b4078b818231dd0532014f0ccdf608b111fc2f8871be0137ffb59214266</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:04:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises--19b14e275677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Glacial collapse leaves 3,000 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b09a025583b7d3b5da31db5dd632af856ebf23b55ce9891d054bf165a7aa5670</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing--bf2b04c1f945.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Death toll rises as 3,000 remain missing in Nepal, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc534c9e31271f2e8e55f343a9c8aa452751ee154ed6bdc6416c0b20d4b9ed9a</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:37:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china--6a7e3695e252.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin, Xi set for Central Asia summit as Russia and China seek to counter Western influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d70b2cc4e6b9c10c30a0eb7f94efaecb4463eae58cdd5575a78863baccbf400f</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T05:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence--62e15ee5debd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping are due in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for a two-day summit, joined by the leaders of Iran and India. The gathering comes as the group seeks to project a united front amid wars in Ukraine and Iran and growing tensions with the West.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal begins mass burials as flood death toll surpasses 780</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e65c1a0e9457dba467316a05114784462e3c8a760c2db8acf491f2fad676d5b0</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T04:59:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises--8e74f89e9cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Sunday began temporarily burying some of the hundreds of bodies recovered from devastating floods after taking DNA samples and marking the remains so families can identify and retrieve them later. Rescue efforts entered a fifth day, with heavy overnight rain and rising rivers hampering attempts to reach hydropower workers believed to be trapped in tunnels. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Missing toll from Nepal, China flood nears 3,000 as race for survivors continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b01f596c8cfdfb9323577434e403bd8bc051b644e7489dcb7a40ca6bfc64a8a6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:12:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues--011d0bbdf6ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues" /><summary type="html">Rescuers in Nepal and China on Saturday continued to search for the nearly 3,000 people missing after devastating flooding along the border with China engulfed entire villages earlier this week. At least 682 bodies were recovered in both countries, including 675 in Nepal and seven in China.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Extremely risky operations’: Rescuers work amid threat of river banks bursting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6410e510402d44552c274860c1e3ca506ca5f0cef00f92dac21b21e40f9af06d</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:22:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/extremely-risky-operations-rescuers-work-amid-threat-of-river-banks-bursting--71fe5095c630.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/extremely-risky-operations-rescuers-work-amid-threat-of-river-banks-bursting" /><summary type="html">Nearly 3,000 people remained missing on Saturday, while 682 deaths had been confirmed after flash floods and landslides hit the Nepal-Tibet border. Rescue operations remain risky as a lake formed upstream by the floods threatens to burst its banks. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rescue operations ongoing as death toll continues to rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:665b4a928dc23997f217438ae6db199a7de46602a022af8a8da0d0835bec46c6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:37:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rescue-operations-ongoing-as-death-toll-continues-to-rise--58c55377d6ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rescue-operations-ongoing-as-death-toll-continues-to-rise" /><summary type="html">Most arrive with nothing except the clothes they are wearing. As rescue efforts in communities buried by catastrophic flash floods along the border between Nepal and China entered their fourth day Saturday, authorities continued finding survivors and transporting them to safety. At relief centers, as some arrive, families wait anxiously for news of their loved ones as the death toll and the number of people unaccounted for continued to rise.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepali army uses helicopters to rescue flood survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f10819f80514847599e31708cbc9e9878df6beb01825d20e2ae0a729ff6834d6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:32:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepali-army-uses-helicopters-to-rescue-flood-survivors--db6798aa1af5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepali-army-uses-helicopters-to-rescue-flood-survivors" /><summary type="html">With roads damaged by the deadly floods, the Nepali army is using helicopters to carry out rescue operations and transport survivors to safety. Meanwhile, skies remain overcast, with more rain expected in the coming hours, raising concerns about further flooding. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal army races to rescue more than 100 trapped in hydropower tunnel after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c8195d26823b88c0e10c32664e67eb1737e49d5803aa1bceb865f9581b69757</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-army-races-to-rescue-more-than-100-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnel-after-floods--2034486870f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-army-races-to-rescue-more-than-100-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnel-after-floods" /><summary type="html">Nepali army rescue teams were using drilling equipment on Saturday seeking to rescue more than 100 people trapped inside a hydropower tunnel, three days after devastating floods struck the site.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN, Nepal warn of climate threat after flood death toll tops 680</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476f9599b7bfa4cc771c6f197109a3994c3ec4b811e042c2e2fd4979338d70ac</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T05:06:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-nepal-tibet-floods-live-death-toll-passes-600-nearly-2-500-people-still-missing--1f3e59acefbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-nepal-tibet-floods-live-death-toll-passes-600-nearly-2-500-people-still-missing" /><summary type="html">Nepal's foreign minister and the UN climate chief on Saturday warned of the growing threat from climate change to the Himalayas, three days after devastating floods swept along the border with China, engulfing entire villages. At least 675 people were killed in Nepal, according to the country's disaster authority. Another seven people were confirmed dead in Tibet, Chinese state media reported. Read our blog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Families cling to hope as nearly 1,000 remain missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36fd687e779bd721ba86bfd563b4c2f7faf6ac393578b74d153ee8aac5a93907</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-families-cling-to-hope-as-nearly-1-000-remain-missing--d90124379841.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-families-cling-to-hope-as-nearly-1-000-remain-missing" /><summary type="html">Nepal's confirmed death toll has risen to at least 538, but families are still searching hospitals and disaster zones in the hope their loved ones will be found alive, with nearly 1,000 people still missing. More than 3,700 people have been rescued so far, though destroyed roads, bridges and thick mud continue to hamper search efforts.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Relief camp shelters grieving families</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54b0e88f8da2f0d9486ed10d25f9cb3de349273cedd64a91adb40dd94804ce6e</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-relief-camp-shelters-grieving-families--251bec211f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-relief-camp-shelters-grieving-families" /><summary type="html">Around 500 people are sheltering at a monastery-turned-relief camp in northern Kathmandu, where many families are still in shock after losing their homes and loved ones in the devastating Nepal floods. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports from the camp as rescue teams continue searching for nearly 1,000 missing people, with operations set to continue through the night.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rescuers grapple with a mountain of challenges after the Nepal-Tibet floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9cd7047fa17c4b873c13bd2a4ab720bfa037ee39f11b9cd2b61e0e134eada28</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-rescuers-grapple-with-mountain-of-challenges-after-the-nepal-tibet-floods--bbaa37403151.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-rescuers-grapple-with-mountain-of-challenges-after-the-nepal-tibet-floods" /><summary type="html">Emergency services are rushing to find survivors and treat the wounded after a devastating flash flood on the border of Nepal and Tibet on Wednesday killed more than 500 people, with over a thousand still missing. But the remote and rugged terrain, as well as the risk of further flooding from upstream lakes formed by piles of debris, make their work as delicate as it is dangerous.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods explained: The chain of events behind the disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dce178b4b3b35029f633a6b96de4bb58f5aaeda72c5da880be27b0b8bc6e9a7</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:48:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-explained-the-chain-of-events-behind-the-disaster--5ab0173979c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-explained-the-chain-of-events-behind-the-disaster" /><summary type="html">A glacier broke apart. An ice and rock avalanche followed. Then came an earthquake, before a landslide triggered devastating floods that tore through kilometres of valley. This is what happened along the Nepal-China border, where rescue teams are still trying to recover survivors 48 hours after the catastrophe. FRANCE 24 breaks down the chain of events and the scientific explanations behind the disaster.</summary></entry><entry><title>Japan's controversial WWII heroes: How one kamikaze pilot escaped certain death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:340f0c3c821b9e0e03ca7462b4148846aa443ad146f947e9865469577948ba0c</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:42:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260828-japan-s-controversial-wwii-heroes-how-one-kamikaze-pilot-escaped-certain-death--ad0c943dfef7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260828-japan-s-controversial-wwii-heroes-how-one-kamikaze-pilot-escaped-certain-death" /><summary type="html">Towards the end of World War II, as US troops advanced across the Pacific, Japan resorted to a desperate strategy: kamikaze attacks. Thousands of Japanese pilots, with an average age of just 21, were ordered to crash their explosive-laden planes into enemy ships. More than 3,800 pilots gave up their lives, killing over 7,000 allied naval personnel. Our reporter Mélodie Sforza met one of the last surviving former kamikaze pilots.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7457a91c6666d2c0b338a7e2ed72af30c24d62d098bb7dcf890f9e92dd6dfa1c</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel--4ef4567d0335.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel" /><summary type="html">Nepali soldiers rescued around 100 people trapped inside a flooded hydropower tunnel as the death toll from the Nepal-China floods continued to climb, with more than 1,500 people still missing. Rescue efforts were briefly suspended over fears that an overflowing landslide lake could trigger more flooding, while families across the disaster zone continue searching for loved ones.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Ran for our lives': Flood survivors recount terrifying escape from Nepal-Tibet disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:343951e9ff4af837f74aebb6b6cc225e81f938c991afb8f47db68bfe5962df03</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T11:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-ran-for-our-lives-flood-survivors-recount-terrifying-escape-from-nepal-tibet-disaster--9062a87ff517.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-ran-for-our-lives-flood-survivors-recount-terrifying-escape-from-nepal-tibet-disaster" /><summary type="html">Survivors of the catastrophic flash floods in Nepal and Tibet, some still missing friends and family members, shared harrowing accounts of their escape from raging floodwaters that brought devastation to the Himalayan border region, leaving more than 550 people dead and some 1,500 missing.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
